00:04:55.620 --> 00:05:02.400
So how does this wind tunnel get air to travel at&nbsp;
mach 7? On one end is a big old vacuum chamber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.680
and on the other is a pressurized tube, the&nbsp;
two sides are separated by a metal diaphragm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.600
that is designed to pop at a target pressure&nbsp;
differential. You would think that increasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:17.520
the pressure would increase the speed of air&nbsp;
traveling between the sections, but it doesn’t.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.720
Dr. Combs:&nbsp;

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:24.360
one other little nuance is people think&nbsp;
that you can, if you increase the pressure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:27.240
that should increase the mach number.&nbsp;
Right? That kind of conceptually makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.891
sense. Our Mach number is actually fixed by the&nbsp;
geometry. It's just all about expansion ratio.

00:05:31.891 --> 00:05:31.906
