Uh, so changing pressure just changes the reynolds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:39.780
number and the, the mass flux and the equivalent&nbsp;
altitude that you have. But the Mach number is 7.2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.040
basically, regardless of what diaphragm that&nbsp;
we use. Um, and that's fixed by the shape.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:50.580
